                "reasoning_content": "We need to evaluate the provided solution to the problem: \"Consider a 2025×2025 grid of unit squares. Matilda wishes to place on the grid some rectangular tiles, possibly of difference sizes, such that each side of every tile lies on a grid line and every unit square is covered by at most one tile. Determine the minimum number of tiles Matilda needs to place so that each row and each column of the grid has exactly one unit square that is not covered by any tile.\"\n\nThe solution given:\n\n- Defines n=2025.\n\n- Uncovered squares: one per row and column, thus a permutation.\n\n- Lower bound: defines L (cells left of holes) and R (cells right of holes). Argues each column j (1 to n-1) is the rightmost column of a distinct tile covering L, thus at least n-1 tiles for L. Similarly for R, at least n-1 tiles. So total at least 2n-2.\n\n- Construction: identity permutation (holes on diagonal). For each row i, place left tile covering columns 1..i-1 (if i>1) and right tile covering columns i+1..n (if i<n). So left tiles for rows 2..n (n-1 left tiles) and right tiles for rows 1..n-1 (n-1 right tiles). Total 2n-2 tiles. Works.\n\n- Concludes answer = 2*2025-2 = 4048.\n\nWe need to evaluate according to hierarchical decision tree.\n\nFirst, identify problem type: It's an optimization problem (minimum number of tiles). So it's MINIMIZATION.\n\nThus Level 1: For optimization problems, we do not check answer correctness (i.e., we cannot claim it's wrong). We only check for arithmetic errors or constraint violations. The answer is 4048. Check arithmetic: 2*2025 = 4050, minus 2 = 4048. That's correct. No arithmetic error.\n\nCheck constraint violations: Does the construction satisfy constraints? The construction uses horizontal tiles of height 1 covering all cells left and right of diagonal holes. Tiles are axis-aligned, each tile's interior is disjoint (since each tile occupies a distinct row and distinct column intervals). Does any tile cov